# coverage=1.3: ClaimRecord, BenefitStatement, DenialNotice, AppealRecord interfaces added
# health=2.3: ProcedureRecord rdfType and predicates corrected from clinical: to health: namespace (REC-5)
# core=3.0: AIExtractionActivity, AIDiscardedExtraction, SocialHistoryConsent interfaces added
# clinical=1.8: ClinicalSocialHistoryRecord interface added (EHR-extracted, 42 CFR Part 2)
# clinical=1.8: Medication RDF type and predicates migrated from health: to clinical: namespace
# core=3.1: AdvisoryApplicationActivity, AIGenerationActivity, GenerationTrigger added
# core=3.2: appliedTriplesCount property added
# core=3.3: AIAsserted provenance leaf and ProxyAgent (caregiver-proxy) added
# health=2.4: SocialHistoryRecord (consumer-reported) added; distinct from clinical:SocialHistoryRecord
# clinical=1.9: cascade:AIExtracted accepted as a dataProvenance value on clinical records
#
# core=3.4: pod export manifest. All 32 terms implemented. ExportManifest,
#     RecordSummary and InteractionScenario models + TYPE_MAPPING entries, all 26
#     uncontested properties in PROPERTY_PREDICATES, full serialize/deserialize
#     and JSON-LD context coverage. dcat and void registered in NAMESPACES
#     because ExportManifest is rdfs:subClassOf dcat:Dataset and RecordSummary
#     rdfs:subClassOf void:Dataset with every count rdfs:subPropertyOf
#     void:entities; the VoID subproperty axioms themselves live in the ontology
#     and are NOT re-asserted by this SDK. cascade:date, cascade:notes and
#     cascade:loincCode collide with the health:/clinical: spellings this SDK
#     already writes: both spellings are ACCEPTED ON READ, and which one is
#     written is decided per record type (TYPE_PREDICATE_OVERRIDES). Verified
#     byte-exact against conformance fixtures pod-002 and pod-004.
# core=3.4: sourceType, dataTypes and version are registered as predicates only.
#     They are emitted on prov:Agent device-source subjects, for which the core
#     ontology defines no class, so there is no model to attach them to.
# health=2.5: the five clinical record classes were ALREADY supported; v2.5
#     defined what this SDK was already emitting. Closed the real gaps: the 4
#     missing daily-snapshot properties (activeEnergyKcal, exerciseMinutes,
#     standHours, durationHours), the DailyActivitySnapshot / DailySleepSnapshot
#     models and type mappings, health:sleepQuality emitted and parsed as an IRI
#     over the 4 named individuals, and the 6 wellness container classes as
#     WELLNESS_CONTAINER_SUBCLASSES + isHealthProfileType(). All 40 v2.5
#     properties are registered and audited by test. Verified byte-exact against
#     conformance fixtures dailyactivity-001/002 and dailysleep-001/002.
# health=2.5: the wellness containers are CONSTANTS ONLY — a subclass map and a
#     predicate. The eight history-container object properties
#     (restingHeartRateHistory, dailyActivityHistory, ...) and the reading
#     classes they range over are still unmodelled here; this release does not
#     claim to serialize a health:HealthProfile.
# clinical=1.10: hasEncounter, indicationReference and linkedCondition added as
#     IRI-valued edges; the deprecated linkedConditionIds literal is still read.
# clinical=1.11: indicationReference carried on Procedure and
#     MedicationAdministration as well as Medication, matching the widened domain.
# clinical=1.12: parsedIndicationReference added as a separate field, kept
#     distinguishable from indicationReference so a consumer can label a derived
#     match differently from a stated one.
# clinical=1.13: the 4 deprecated classes are read, never written.
#     DEPRECATED_TYPE_ALIASES maps clinical:LabResult/Condition/Allergy/
#     Immunization to their health: successors and deserialize() accepts both
#     spellings; TYPE_MAPPING has no entry for any of them, so nothing here can
#     emit one. The unambiguous clinical: spellings of their properties are also
#     accepted on read — accepting the class but dropping its data would be a
#     silent data loss. clinical:value, clinical:unit, clinical:interpretation
#     and clinical:severity are deliberately NOT aliased: three already resolve
#     to a VitalSign field and the fourth would collide with cascade:severity,
#     and a reverse predicate map has no record-type context to disambiguate.
